her feet have barely touched the ground  since winning the u.s open being a grand  slam champion brings many extra demands  but for emma radhakanu her life really  changed after wimbledon wimbledon was  the first moment for me where you know i  was really being like competitive on a  global scale i feel and uh obviously  there was so much excitement going on  and adrenaline like i've never felt  before because that was the first time  and uh i mean i was so so proud and  happy but being at home playing in front  of a home crowd i think it was such a  special feeling and especially out there  on court one it was the biggest court  i've ever played on so the way that i  went out there i feel i was quite  nervous but  yeah i just absolutely loved it once i  got out there and the home crowd was  just such a such a great pleasure to  play in front of  and talk us through the us open which  you sort of touched on but you know how  did the three weeks evolve that you were  there competing you know did you have to  keep upgrading your goals  well i  it was so funny i i arrived in new york  just just hoping to get through  qualifying maybe i mean i was pretty  tired but um  i  i just had the most amazing time and i  think nikita that i was honestly so  focused on on the day that the time flew  by and uh  it went so fast by the end of it me and  my team were just having a great time  and for me i was like i don't want to  leave yet you know i want to stay and  and then it was getting to the latter  stages of the tournament and i was i was  really thinking oh but what if like  you're here like you can you know why  not you must have got more and more  excited though as you went on and how  did you sort of keep that  under control it was great because out  there i had a great circle of people who  are close to me and we we just went  about every single day as normal you  know that we weren't getting  into  any of the really extra excitement it  was just between us you know keeping the  routines the exact same thing and i  think that's what really worked you know  everything was the same and no one made  a big deal out of it  are you superstitious did you have to  sort of keep wearing the same socks  well i actually wasn't until maybe like  the last week where i was thinking like  okay i was having pokey for dinner every  single night and  then by the for three weeks  and then by the end i was i just kept it  the same because i didn't want to take  any chances what do you think about when  you when you think of new york you know  what pops into your head after what you  achieved is it are you proud are you  still slightly in disbelief you know  what it what is it  yeah i think that the best memories i  have of new york as is just of the  amount of fun i had out there and  i i definitely felt like i faced my own  sort of obstacles and the way i overcame  those and for example the first time i  stepped out onto ash i was quite nervous  and i didn't realize until i really  started i got off to a slow start but  then the way that i overcame that and by  the end i was completely thriving out  there in front of so many people you  can't win every match as a tennis player  you know everybody knows that but how do  you cope with the raised expectations of  other people outside the sport now that  you've you've won a grand slam yeah i  feel like people are going to have  opinions and expectations of me but i  don't really think about that at all and  to me it doesn't really matter the only  the only thing that matters to me is my  expectations of myself and what i want  to achieve or what i want to get out of  the day and it's it's just about  improving you know seeing yourself get  better what did you learn about yourself  in this year  in this year i learned i was pretty  resilient i'd say  um because it there were like a lot of  ups and downs i mean of course i didn't  play tennis  for three months at all at the beginning  of the year like i didn't pick up a  racquet and i was sitting my a levels  and  you know i was like thinking when is my  next tournament going to be and then at  wimbledon i had an incredible experience  and then yeah i  physically  was tired at the end of it and uh  yeah but i bounced back from that went  out to the states and i had a great  swing so it's just up and down but uh  being resilient and smoothing out that  curve do you have any non-tennis targets  i mean i don't know if you can drive for  example  are there any things you want to do  not related to tennis  yeah there are many many things i mean i  have my driver's license but i'm like a  big adrenaline junkie and like motor  sports fan but um i'd say  maybe get my motorbike license i hope or  you know something really like speedy  and fun and just continue to  like really push to push the boundaries  of that because i find it i just get  such a thrill from it somewhat 2021 in a  word  2021 was a surprise  and a journey those two i couldn't pick  2022 will be emma's first full year on  the tour so there are many journeys  ahead but she's proud of how far she's  come  jackie beltral sky sports
 

